  "rule": "Each one-cell-thick rectangular frame encloses a strip that repeats a short tile along its long axis except for a few corrupted cells; the output keeps background and frames and rewrites every strip from its (majority) periodic tile, removing the stray cells.",
  "scope": "Supported: 1-4 framed panels stacked (horizontal strips) or side by side (vertical strips), shared periodic length 8-26, per-panel strip width 1-4, minimal periods 2-6 from stripe / shifted-stripe / block / diagonal-sweep / zigzag / random tile families, one or two pattern colours plus the background colour inside each strip, margin 1-2 and gap 1-2, 1-6 corruptions per panel as isolated spots or a shifted segment (as in train 2). Deliberately not supported: square strip interiors (orientation undefined), periods with fewer than three repeats, more than one corruption per period class, corruptions in the frame colour, panels with different lengths, frames thicker than one cell, panels without any corruption, grids where the background is not the strict majority colour.",
  "constraints": [
    "Frame colour differs from background and from every pattern/corruption colour, so each frame is its own connected ring object.",
    "Strip width is strictly smaller than the periodic length (long axis unambiguous).",
    "Length >= 3 * period, so every period class has at least three members; each corruption occupies a distinct (residue, column) class, hence the majority of every class equals the true tile and the mismatch count equals the number of corruptions.",
    "The true period is the unique minimiser of the majority-mismatch count: all smaller candidate periods have strictly more mismatches and all larger ones at least as many (ties only resolve to the smaller true period), verified per panel on the corrupted strip.",
    "Tile has minimal cyclic period exactly p (not reducible) and contains at least one non-background cell.",
    "Background colour is the strict most frequent colour of the input grid.",
    "No 4-connected same-colour component outside frames/background is a hollow ring with bounding box >= 3x3, so frames are the only ring objects (checked on input and output).",
    "Panels are separated by at least one background cell and surrounded by a background margin; every panel has at least one corruption so input != output."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Validity relies on a local period-uniqueness check (majority mismatch per candidate period) on each corrupted strip; outputs themselves are generated from the latent tile, never from that check.",
    "Grid dimensions are derived from the sampled layout rather than sampled directly; the rule intrinsically fixes them given panels, margin, gap and length.",
    "Corruption colours are drawn only from the panel palette plus background, matching the originals; off-palette corruption colours are not generated.",
    "The reference's objects/background helpers are assumed to be per-colour connected components and most-common colour respectively; scenes are constrained so either 4- or 8-connectivity yields the same frames."
  ],
